es and calories"}, {"id": "fbad09e9-43e0-40b8-932d-f8cec45c3ede", "type": "concept", "title": "Percent Daily Value, sodium, added sugar, fiber, and saturated fat"}, {"id": "72532d6f-c821-4fb8-9c90-2d6f43a4c107", "type": "concept", "title": "Ingredient lists, claims, and front-of-package labeling"}]}, {"id": "4f612b1b-b391-453c-8bcb-2311d7c877f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meal planning skills", "description": "Students learn practical planning for real life constraints.", "children": [{"id": "439743f1-bd92-421c-bee2-e08086ef79e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Balanced meals and snacks"}, {"id": "f96ffbb5-8abd-492b-a572-1c661977a3d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Grocery planning, cooking basics, and leftovers"}, {"id": "2f11582e-5be9-4fa7-8365-bf30ab46e7d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Portion awareness and mindful eating"}]}]}, {"id": "75e45e83-31c7-4895-a250-8e62767e1c6d", "type": "topic", "title": "Nutrition Assessment, Diet Analysis, and Goal Setting", "description": "This module teaches how to collect, interpret, and communicate nutrition information without overclaiming or stigmatizing.", "children": [{"id": "6fb1e7cb-4bf0-4b9e-930a-4af0419b6d22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dietary assessment", "description": "Students learn common ways to estimate intake and the limits of each method.", "children": [{"id": "2bd07869-e79e-436f-a255-40979c4007ce", "type": "concept", "title": "24-hour recalls, food records, and food frequency questionnaires"}, {"id": "cdcc4e6d-711f-4cc7-b0b0-e2ad02bae6a6", "type": "concept", "title": "Diet analysis software and nutrient databases"}, {"id": "ccb238b2-ec93-46ea-99b5-36b00afc75b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Recall bias, underreporting, and context"}]}, {"id": "f161ec50-bc48-48f9-ab72-095ac86a8dc3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Health and body data", "description": "Students interpret nutrition-related data with caution and respect.", "children": [{"id": "b3f9ed54-ae1b-416b-aed0-2c973e7b62e4", "type": "concept", "title": "Anthropometrics and body composition basics"}, {"id": "2289a135-005f-44e5-9d9a-4c13ccb4febf", "type": "concept", "title": "Labs, blood pressure, medications, and clinical context"}, {"id": "91855152-de12-4f72-8f36-c71b7a6514fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Screening versus diagnosis"}]}, {"id": "0b282750-1476-4082-bf2c-f8a9463cb68a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Goal setting", "description": "Students turn assessment into realistic, measurable, person-centered goals.", "children": [{"id": "fd9ee31a-d69f-4d84-a66b-b2334d8245dd", "type": "concept", "title": "SMART goals and readiness to change"}, {"id": "5b4438d5-e67e-44fb-a51b-5c9ce9e19a44", "type": "concept", "title": "Tracking, feedback, and self-monitoring"}, {"id": "3de2cb4f-5ba6-4487-80e8-71535c178aca", "type": "concept", "title": "When to refer to a registered dietitian or clinician"}]}]}, {"id": "98006442-c028-408d-bb34-84b08d85cff0", "type": "topic", "title": "Lifecycle Nutrition: Pregnancy, Infancy, Childhood, Adolescence, Adulthood, and Aging", "description": "Students learn how nutrient priorities change across life stages and how wellness guidance must fit developmental context.", "children": [{"id": "b893d852-1e3a-4d88-8c1a-f2f798b979aa", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pregnancy, lactation, and infancy", "description": "Students learn early-life nutrition priorities that shape growth and long-term health.", "children": [{"id": "f2b18602-db06-4d43-b96f-c36d14bdade5", "type": "concept", "title": "Folate, iron, iodine, DHA, and gestational weight guidance"}, {"id": "8601e421-4d8a-4c86-93b4-d8785cc11a8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Breastfeeding, formula, and complementary foods"}, {"id": "71416108-47af-48e6-84e0-eff5a4fa27b6", "type": "concept", "title": "Food safety and high-risk nutrients"}]}, {"id": "da04e41b-fe14-46dc-96b0-1d3c926b1815", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Childhood and adolescence", "description": "Students study nutrition for growth, development, activity, and family routines.", "child