e": "subtopic", "title": "Hydration and recovery", "description": "Students learn practical recovery strategies grounded in fluid, electrolyte, sleep, and meal timing.", "children": [{"id": "2f219652-9aef-477b-8603-0f66504383c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Sweat loss and sodium replacement"}, {"id": "0a24460e-0c21-42dc-9fe1-7e35272ae169", "type": "concept", "title": "Protein distribution and muscle repair"}, {"id": "77bd6335-bc6c-41b3-8d7b-360476e0a613", "type": "concept", "title": "Recovery meals, rest, and training adaptation"}]}, {"id": "ef2523a7-4209-4f19-be50-e717d05b2f2a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance supplements", "description": "Students evaluate supplements through evidence, safety, and ethical risk.", "children": [{"id": "f2e9ae32-54c7-4a6b-aa24-628a1d8340f9", "type": "concept", "title": "Creatine, caffeine, protein powders, nitrate, and beta-alanine overview"}, {"id": "16fae5a6-4eb4-42d6-8f3e-7a946daf595b", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplement 411 and contamination risk"}, {"id": "5dd42287-1bcd-48ed-ba17-94860f53eb44", "type": "concept", "title": "Special populations and contraindications"}]}]}, {"id": "bc616536-33af-4104-8e6c-1b376c644cef", "type": "topic", "title": "Diet and Chronic Disease Prevention", "description": "Students study how dietary patterns influence cardiometabolic, gastrointestinal, renal, skeletal, and cancer-related risk over time.", "children": [{"id": "41f48e5e-31f4-4d93-b5b3-9f8b9faafc4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cardiometabolic health", "description": "Students learn how dietary patterns influence heart disease, hypertension, diabetes, and dyslipidemia.", "children": [{"id": "191232be-2573-41a0-9a94-6014667a440b", "type": "concept", "title": "DASH, Mediterranean, fiber-rich, and low-sodium patterns"}, {"id": "3b2c8c11-5796-45a6-a492-854798d2d904", "type": "concept", "title": "Blood glucose, insulin resistance, and diabetes prevention"}, {"id": "4d5b5d36-c02d-4c50-9889-956ecdbc988a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lipids, blood pressure, inflammation, and vascular health"}]}, {"id": "1fff67b4-f26b-4a3a-a83b-84398bff97ae", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gastrointestinal, renal, and bone health", "description": "Students connect nutrition to common organ-system risks.", "children": [{"id": "870a4961-36ce-40e9-8795-340a40a9c1f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Fiber, constipation, reflux, IBS, and inflammatory bowel disease overview"}, {"id": "8f4e24d7-6030-4b60-8b71-f41b48d0aa15", "type": "concept", "title": "Kidney stone and chronic kidney disease nutrition basics"}, {"id": "1bd7bf8c-2b7b-4ac9-9f06-7a79e5ed5acb", "type": "concept", "title": "Calcium, vitamin D, protein, and osteoporosis prevention"}]}, {"id": "eb6ed537-c7aa-466e-b916-543078ef6623", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cancer and immune-related prevention", "description": "Students examine prevention guidance without overstating what diet can do.", "children": [{"id": "566dbc6b-68c1-48c2-a1e7-f07b53e816e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Alcohol, processed meat, fiber, body composition, and cancer risk"}, {"id": "3c155be5-5e5e-4a0f-993f-a237864828d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Immune function and adequacy"}, {"id": "fd04e104-5713-4498-b58a-5758536c8541", "type": "concept", "title": "Survivorship nutrition and referral boundaries"}]}]}, {"id": "d28f17aa-b311-4e5c-8d60-5b5381fe99f2", "type": "topic", "title": "Weight, Body Composition, Metabolic Health, and Non-Stigmatizing Care", "description": "This module develops a careful, humane approach to weight and metabolic health that avoids shame and simplistic advice.", "children": [{"id": "4950e534-e300-44e2-9250-65fd6adb438a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Body composition", "description": "Students learn body composition concepts and measurement limits.", "children": [{"id": "0084f971-b1a4-410e-890e-ee20a103b2e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Fat mass, lean mass, bone, and water"}, {"id": "47dbeb0a-e458-4bef-83c7-8dccd7ca2c12", "type": "concept", "title": "BMI strengths and limits"}, {"id": "2aaf9125-5a02-49e1-9f80-62e545254c85", "type": "concept", "title": "Waist circumference, DEXA, BIA, and skinfold overview"}]}, {"id": "7d0cd929-2dc2-40f8-9cb8-95e9f638e78d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Weight regulation", "description": "Students study weight change as biology plus behavior plus environment.", "children": [{"id": "b36d8a86-7150-4a10-b5aa-bdaf654fa8b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Energy intake, expenditure, appetite, sleep, stress, medications, and genetics"}, {"id": "59db356b-67e0-411c-901d-8c6366f82dd5", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight cycling and adaptive thermogenesis"}, {"id": "b57dbe92-c8cf-4a89-8d0d-915a9290d654", "type": "concept", "title": "Metabolic health at different body sizes"}]}, {"id": "3ec309c9-774b-4cfb-b346-7b6dfdd45bba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Respectful care", "description": "Students practice language and strategies that support health without shame.", "children": [{"id": "74ce21f4-3073-4cc6-a585-b2e2aa6c6c94", "type": "concept", "title": "Weight stigma and bias"}, {"id": "b2b58da5-c139-44b2-a114-0a744f328971", "type": "concept", "title": "Non-diet and health-at-every-size-informed concepts"}, {"id": "b366069b-5ccf-492f-91ab-b832f6615461", "type": "concept", "title": "Eating disorder screening and referral awareness"}]}]}, {"id": "f057aed8-9599-4719-9cfa-194dac42e4fd", "type": "topic", "title": "Gut Health, Food Safety, Allergies, and Intolerances", "description": "Students learn how digestion, the microbiome, safe food handling, and adverse food reactions affect everyday wellness.", "children": [{"id": "5949a5bc-fdfa-4474-8dfa-dc5d300bc75a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Gut microbiome", "description": "Students learn what is known, what is plausible, and what remains uncertain about microbiome health.", "children": [{"id": "5ab31748-4602-42d4-8f6b-d8c1a0153850", "type": "concept", "title": "Prebiotics, probiotics, fermented foods, and fiber"}, {"id": "dc4b11be-9f47-47f6-9132-76fd5c7fd1cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Microbial diversity and short-chain fatty acids"}, {"id": "c7f48da2-4da3-4c76-9fe9-0d065acf16f1", "type": "concept", "title": "Marketing claims and evidence limits"}]}, {"id": "42a75736-9c61-4cbb-857e-aab054a5e417", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food safety", "description": "Students learn prevention of foodborne illness in homes, institutions, and community settings.", "children": [{"id": "f9f54667-fe79-44b4-8d97-6e9e1837ef2f", "type": "concept", "title": "Clean, separate, cook, and chill"}, {"id": "20a203f8-8f4c-4f75-85f8-00c834463198", "type": "concept", "title": "High-risk foods and populations"}, {"id": "52d105ea-6d12-47fd-ac72-1eca9e88bcc5", "type": "concept", "title": "Food storage, cross-contamination, and outbreak awareness"}]}, {"id": "92aec3f2-d253-487f-b3a3-ecf0930bcf9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Allergies and intolerances", "description": "Students distinguish immune reactions from intolerances and preferences.", "children": [{"id": "d3e52e23-f71d-494f-a123-2517d454565c", "type": "concept", "title": "Food allergy and anaphylaxis awareness"}, {"id": "786704b1-1fed-48a6-b1e8-3813771333d0", "type": "concept", "title": "Lactose intolerance, celiac disease, and gluten-related claims"}, {"id": "ec760b3f-4925-4cb2-88b4-66ca2a89dad8", "type": "concept", "title": "Elimination diets, reintroduction, and referral"}]}]}, {"id": "aa38a20c-7baa-453c-9f2f-a4fd41a68c14", "type": "topic", "title": "Mental Health, Sleep, Stress, and Nutrition", "description": "This topic connects nutrition with mood, cognition, sleep, stress physiology, and lifestyle patterns while preserving appropriate evidence boundaries.", "children": [{"id": "7b1d7858-8149-4942-ab0e-685e399d32ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Mood and cognition", "description": "Students examine how diet quality can support brain function while avoiding simplistic claims.", "children": [{"id": "ba1f3e90-acb1-4454-91e4-8928448629b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Omega-3 fats, B vi